  "title": "Ignition Cut",
  "user_description": "Independent ignition-cut limiter with RPM hysteresis, optional fixed injector pulse width and an optional fixed ignition angle in a configurable RPM region below the cut limit. Provides shared timing and combustion-observation recovery for Launch Control V14.",
  "description": "This retained revision uses E847-E84A, which overlaps native roughness/reference arrays on its exact supported image. Detection/removal only; use ignition_cut_v16_ms411. MS41.1 Ignition Cut V14 retains its predecessor's cut request and release owners and adds a separate RPM-band timing owner. Standalone and launch ignition retard are active within their configured regions on rising and falling RPM, independent of cut hysteresis. Spark cut retains priority. No hold timer is added. E849 retains the qualified observation-state ABI; E84A distinguishes fuel-launch, ignition-launch and standalone timing sources. Only final timing publishes these states. Guards use read-only eligibility and native accepted-sample/misfire recovery. Genuine native fault and knock protections remain effective; DTC100 and electrical diagnostics are not suppressed. Final timing hooks and qualification are owned by this shared engine, so standalone retard does not require Launch Control. Launch eligibility requires its exact native hook to be installed. New retard angles default Off; an erased RPM range initializes to 192 RPM. Existing tuned bytes are preserved.",
